# Build-context excludes for `docker build -f build/docker/Dockerfile .`
# (Phase 32, Unit 32.10). Docker reads the .dockerignore at the build-context
# root; the gateway image is built with the repository root as context, so this
# file lives here. It keeps the context small and, critically, keeps the
# workspace files out of the build (gdev is consumed from the vendor tree with
# GOWORK=off + -mod=vendor; ../gdev does not exist in the container).

# Version control and CI metadata.
.git/
.github/

# The Go workspace MUST NOT enter the build: it `use`s ../gdev, which is absent
# in the container. The build ignores the workspace and uses vendor/ instead.
go.work
go.work.sum

# Local-only docs and planning material.
internal-docs/

# devenv / direnv / nix build artifacts — large and never needed in the image.
.devenv/
.devenv.flake.nix
.direnv/
result
result-*

# Claude Code / agent scratch and local config.
.claude/

# Test scratch, temp dirs, and ad-hoc runners.
tmp*/
tmp-*
*.tmp
run-e2e.sh
gotest.sh
docs/e2e-runbook-comprehensive.md

# Editor/OS noise.
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
